 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "QbGX5OxaBQAJ",
   "from": "Nicole Torres Tamayo",
   "author": "2bcdc34248a9d24d",
   "date": "2019-02-21T17:10:23Z",
   "subject": "TEST OF HOMOGENEITY OF SLOPES (ALLOMETRY)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi geomorph community :) <br></div><div><br></div><div>I have a dataset with 3 species and I want to test whether the allometry pattern is similar or different between them. For that, I did a test of homogeneity of slopes:</div><div><br></div><div>reg &lt;- procD.allometry(coords~Csize,~species,groups=~species,slope=~Csize,iter=1999,logsz=FALSE, print.progress=FALSE,data=gdf_C1)</div><div><br></div><div>Here I obtain that my 3 species show different slopes (null hypothesis of parallel slopes rejected). <br></div><div><br></div><div>Then, I try to calculate the angle between these slopes using the following function:<br></div><div><br></div><div>advanced.procD.lm(coords ~ Csize,~Csize*species,groups=~species,angle.type = &quot;deg&quot;,slope =~Csize, iter=999,data=gdf_C1)</div><div><br></div><div>However, when I run this analysis, there is no result related to the angles between slopes vectors in my output (although there are other outputs such as slopes, effect sizes, etc) Am I missing something? <br></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you very much in advance.</div><div><br></div><div>All the best,</div><div><br></div><div>Nicole<br></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "yhZINqBhBQAJ",
   "from": "Adams, Dean [EEOBS]",
   "author": "4d71c6e24fb21497",
   "date": "2019-02-21T19:13:10Z",
   "subject": "RE: [geomorph-r-package] TEST OF HOMOGENEITY OF SLOPES (ALLOMETRY)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Nicole,\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><br>\r\nPlease check your output again. After the slopes section, there will be several additional components of comparisons between slopes. One will be ‘Angles between slope vectors’.  That contains the pairwise comparisons between slopes, treated as angles between\r\n them.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><br>\r\nDean<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Dr. Dean C. Adams<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Director of Graduate Education, EEB Program<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Professor<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Iowa State University<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><a href=\"https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485117285000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2TvYmoMD8QdAa3e8wRRAXY\">https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">phone: <a href=\"tel:(515)%20294-3834\" value=\"+15152943834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">515-294-3834</a><u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Nicole Torres Tamayo<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Thursday, February 21, 2019 11:10 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] TEST OF HOMOGENEITY OF SLOPES (ALLOMETRY)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi geomorph community :) <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I have a dataset with 3 species and I want to test whether the allometry pattern is similar or different between them. For that, I did a test of homogeneity of slopes:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">reg &lt;- procD.allometry(coords~Csize,~species,groups=~species,slope=~Csize,iter=1999,logsz=FALSE, print.progress=FALSE,data=gdf_C1)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Here I obtain that my 3 species show different slopes (null hypothesis of parallel slopes rejected).\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Then, I try to calculate the angle between these slopes using the following function:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">advanced.procD.lm(coords ~ Csize,~Csize*species,groups=~species,angle.type = &quot;deg&quot;,slope =~Csize, iter=999,data=gdf_C1)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">However, when I run this analysis, there is no result related to the angles between slopes vectors in my output (although there are other outputs such as slopes, effect sizes, etc) Am I missing something?\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thank you very much in advance.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">All the best,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Nicole<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
