     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Dean</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you very much for your reply. Just one more quick question: the null hypothesis associated to the p-values of the angles between slopes is that the slopes are paralell? <br></div><div><br></div><div>All the best,</div><div><br></div><div>Nicole<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">El jue., 21 feb. 2019 a las 18:10, Nicole Torres Tamayo (&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nicole...@gmail.com</a>&gt;) escribió:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi geomorph community :) <br></div><div><br></div><div>I have a dataset with 3 species and I want to test whether the allometry pattern is similar or different between them. For that, I did a test of homogeneity of slopes:</div><div><br></div><div>reg &lt;- procD.allometry(coords~Csize,~species,groups=~species,slope=~Csize,iter=1999,logsz=FALSE, print.progress=FALSE,data=gdf_C1)</div><div><br></div><div>Here I obtain that my 3 species show different slopes (null hypothesis of parallel slopes rejected). <br></div><div><br></div><div>Then, I try to calculate the angle between these slopes using the following function:<br></div><div><br></div><div>advanced.procD.lm(coords ~ Csize,~Csize*species,groups=~species,angle.type = &quot;deg&quot;,slope =~Csize, iter=999,data=gdf_C1)</div><div><br></div><div>However, when I run this analysis, there is no result related to the angles between slopes vectors in my output (although there are other outputs such as slopes, effect sizes, etc) Am I missing something? <br></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you very much in advance.</div><div><br></div><div>All the best,</div><div><br></div><div>Nicole<br></div></div></div></div>\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
